      "code": "DVWcgROEkzr",
      "kind": "reel",
      "pinned": false,
      "url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DVWcgROEkzr/",
      "caption": "Most people talk about grief like it’s a problem to solve. Either you outrun it, or you collapse under it. As if those are the only endings available.\nBut sometimes it’s neither.\nSometimes it’s quieter than that. It sits beside you at breakfast. It walks with you to work. It shows up in small pauses and familiar songs. It doesn’t disappear, and it doesn’t have to.\nLiving with grief isn’t dramatic. It’s ordinary. It’s learning the shape of it, making space for it, and still choosing to move forward. Not because it hurts less — but because life keeps asking you to participate.\nThere’s a strange strength in that. Not defeating it. Not denying it. Just carrying it gently, and continuing anyway.",
